 {:db/id "9c900468-5124-57f0-aaf9-5d5f900fd66a"
  :question/id #uuid "9c900468-5124-57f0-aaf9-5d5f900fd66a"
  :question/problem "Source question: Canvas Question 3 (question_59459053).\n\nWhat name do we give to $\\det(A-\\lambda I)=0$?"
  :question/answer-fields ["a0a9259c-9e73-51a8-9d5e-02e2b270aa77"]
  :question/worked-solution "**Source terminology issue:** Among the original options, “Characteristic Polynomial” is the intended choice, but the displayed equality is more precisely the **characteristic equation**. The expression $p_A(\\lambda)=\\det(A-\\lambda I)$ is a polynomial in $\\lambda$; setting it equal to zero gives the equation whose roots are the eigenvalues.\n\nIndeed, $A\\vec v=\\lambda\\vec v$ is equivalent to $(A-\\lambda I)\\vec v=\\vec0$. A nonzero solution exists exactly when $A-\\lambda I$ is singular, which is equivalent to $\\det(A-\\lambda I)=0$."
  :db/ensure :question/validate}
